## Multilingual SEO (i18n SEO)

1. **hreflang Tags**
   - Implement hreflang tags for each language version
   - Link alternate language versions
   - Include x-default for default language
   - Ensure correct locale codes (en-US, es-ES, fr-FR)

2. **Implementation Example**
   ```html
   <!-- ✅ DO: Implement hreflang tags -->
   <link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://learninggames.com/en/quiz" />
   <link rel="alternate" hreflang="es" href="https://learninggames.com/es/quiz" />
   <link rel="alternate" hreflang="fr" href="https://learninggames.com/fr/quiz" />
   <link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://learninggames.com/en/quiz" />
   ```

3. **Localized URLs**
   - Use locale-specific URLs (`/en/quiz`, `/es/quiz`, `/fr/quiz`)
   - Consistent URL structure across languages
   - Avoid query parameters for locale (`?lang=en` - not recommended)

4. **Localized Meta Tags**
   - Translate title tags for each language
   - Translate meta descriptions for each language
   - Localize Open Graph tags for each language
   - Use locale-specific keywords

5. **Localized Sitemaps**
   ```xml
   <!-- ✅ DO: Separate sitemaps per language -->
   <?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
   <urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9"
           xmlns:xhtml="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
     <url>
       <loc>https://learninggames.com/en/quiz</loc>
       <xhtml:link rel="alternate" hreflang="es" href="https://learninggames.com/es/quiz" />
       <xhtml:link rel="alternate" hreflang="fr" href="https://learninggames.com/fr/quiz" />
       <xhtml:link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://learninggames.com/en/quiz" />
     </url>
   </urlset>
   ```

6. **Content Localization**
   - Ensure all content is translated (not just UI strings)
   - Translate educational content (quiz questions, explanations)
   - Use locale-specific keywords for each language
   - Consider cultural differences in keyword usage

